.TH MANARADIX-CONFIG 5 "2026-08-14" "manaradix 0.1.3" "File Formats"
.SH NAME
manaradix-config \- configuration file for manaradix
.SH DESCRIPTION
.I /etc/manaradix/config.toml
holds the global settings and per-subvolume snapshot policies of
.BR manaradix (1).
The file is TOML.  If it is missing, built-in defaults apply; it is
created when settings are first saved from the GUI, the CLI, or a setup
profile.
.SH GLOBAL SETTINGS
The
.B [global]
table holds:
.TP
.B default_subvolume
String.  Default subvolume path (default:
.IR "/" ).
.TP
.B snapshot_dir
String.  Snapshot storage directory relative to the mount point
(default:
.IR .snapshots ).
.TP
.B boot_from_snapshot
Boolean.  Enable the GRUB boot-from-snapshot menu
(default: false).
.TP
.B snapshot_before_upgrade
Boolean.  Take a pre-upgrade snapshot of the root subvolume before every
rpm package transaction, via the rpm file trigger shipped with the
package (default: false).
.SH POLICIES
Each
.B [policies."\fI<subvolume>\fR"]
table (the key is the subvolume path, quoted) configures a snapshot
policy.  Keys:
.TP
.B enabled
Boolean.  Whether the policy is active (default: true).
.TP
.B schedule_hourly
Boolean.  Take hourly snapshots (default: false).
.TP
.B schedule_daily
Boolean.  Take daily snapshots (default: true).
.TP
.B schedule_weekly
Boolean.  Take weekly snapshots (default: false).
.TP
.B schedule_monthly
Boolean.  Take monthly snapshots (default: false).
.TP
.B schedule_boot
Boolean.  Snapshot on every boot (default: false).
.SS Retention
The
.B [policies."\fI<subvolume>\fR".retention]
table holds how many snapshots of each tier to keep:
.TP
.B keep_hourly
Integer (default: 10).
.TP
.B keep_daily
Integer (default: 7).
.TP
.B keep_weekly
Integer (default: 4).
.TP
.B keep_monthly
Integer (default: 3).
.TP
.B keep_boot
Integer (default: 5).
.TP
.B keep_pre_upgrade
Integer (default: 3).
.SH TRAY APPLET
The
.B [tray]
table configures the notification-area applet
.RB ( "manaradix tray serve" ).
It is read-only for the applet: the applet never writes the system
config.  Keys:
.TP
.B enabled
Boolean.  Master switch; when false the applet exits immediately
(default: true).
.TP
.B autostart
Boolean.  Whether the applet starts at login from the autostart file
(default: true).
.TP
.B hide_when_ok
Boolean.  When true, the healthy state is passive and Plasma parks
the icon in the hidden tray overflow; when false (default) the icon
stays visible and clickable at all times.
.TP
.B quiet_hours
String.  \fB"HH:MM-HH:MM"\fR window in which notifications (but not the
icon state) are suppressed; start > end crosses midnight, an empty
string disables quiet hours (default: "").
.TP
.B space_enabled
Boolean.  Check free space of every Btrfs filesystem (default: true).
.TP
.B device_enabled
Boolean.  Check the btrfs error counters and (via UDisks2, when
available) the SMART health of the underlying drives (default: true).
.TP
.B retention_enabled
Boolean.  Suggest pruning snapshots that are past their retention tier
budget (default: true).
.TP
.B scrub_enabled
Boolean.  Remind when no scrub is recorded for a filesystem
(default: true).
.TP
.B space_warn_pct
Integer.  Used-space percentage that triggers the warn notification
(default: 85).
.TP
.B space_critical_pct
Integer.  Used-space percentage that triggers the critical notification
(default: 95).
.TP
.B space_interval_min
Integer.  Space check interval in minutes (default: 10).
.TP
.B device_interval_min
Integer.  Device check interval in minutes (default: 60).
.TP
.B retention_interval_min
Integer.  Retention check interval in minutes (default: 1440).
.TP
.B scrub_interval_min
Integer.  Scrub check interval in minutes (default: 60).
.SH SETUP PROFILES
Rather than hand-editing this file, the setup wizard
.RB ( "manaradix setup" )
applies one of the shipped profiles — TOML templates for
.B desktop
(role: desktop), \fBserver\fR (role: server), and \fBkiosk\fR
(role: any).  Templates are searched in
.BR MANARADIX_TEMPLATE_DIRS ,
then the repository
.I data/templates/
when running from a checkout,
.IR /usr/share/manaradix/templates/
(shipped by the RPM), and
.IR /etc/manaradix/templates.d/
(administrator overrides and extras); later directories override
profiles with the same id.
.SH EXAMPLE
.nf
[global]
default_subvolume = "/"
snapshot_dir = ".snapshots"
boot_from_snapshot = true
snapshot_before_upgrade = true

[policies."/"]
enabled = true
schedule_hourly = false
schedule_daily = true
schedule_weekly = true
schedule_monthly = false
schedule_boot = true

[policies."/".retention]
keep_hourly = 10
keep_daily = 7
keep_weekly = 4
keep_monthly = 3
keep_boot = 5
keep_pre_upgrade = 3

[policies."/home"]
enabled = true
schedule_daily = true

[tray]
enabled = true
hide_when_ok = false
quiet_hours = "22:00-07:00"
space_warn_pct = 85
space_critical_pct = 95
space_interval_min = 10
device_interval_min = 60
retention_interval_min = 1440
scrub_interval_min = 60
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR manaradix (1),
.BR btrfs (8),
.BR systemd.timer (5),
.BR udisks (8)
